ent it was used against mike and  sully when they uncovered mr waternoose  and randall's plot  and in monsters university it's implied  that tampering with the mail at the  factory mail room was the reason the  abominable snowman was banished to the  himalayas  and although we see monsters learning  underwater skills at the school of  aquatics in monsters university  if one of them suddenly took on a human  form after emerging from the water we  can assume that the other monsters would  be extremely fearful and suspicious of  them perhaps going so far as to banish  them  and what if the loch ness monster who's  been mentioned as existing in the pixar  universe was one of these monsters  obviously we're talking about fiction  here but perhaps the reason the  existence of nessie has never been  proven  is because it has the ability to come  out of the water and disguise itself as  a human  could the loch ness monster be a monster  human hybrid species like luca and  alberto  legends of the loch ness monster date  back as far as the 6th century  and although loch ness is in scotland  there would be plenty of time for that  monster to use its human form to mix  with the human population  in time for its descendants to end up in  the italian riviera near porto rosso  a monster's inc character who has  somewhat related powers to lucas sea  monsters is the villain randall boggs  who has the power of camouflage to a  much greater degree than real-life  chameleons  randall isn't a shape-shifter but he can  change his skin to blend into his  surroundings and although he initially  can't control his ability in monsters  university  by the time of monsters inc he's in full  charge of his powers  perhaps the sea monsters in lucca then  have a related gene to randall except  they don't seem to be able to fully  control switching it on and off like him  which could even imply the skin changing  power evolves between the time of luca  and monster's inc  an alternate monster's ink c